% The barber paradox: the barber shaves exactly those who do not shave
% themselves.  Does the barber shave the barber?  Russell's paradox as a
% logic program — no stable model exists, and the well-founded model
% leaves precisely shaves(barber, barber) undefined while still settling
% that the barber shaves plato.
%
%   python3 datalog.py programs/03-barber.dl            (rejected)
%   python3 datalog.py --models programs/03-barber.dl   (the semantic verdict)

person(barber).
person(plato).

shaves(barber, X) :- person(X), not shaves(X, X).
